 {"acceptance_criteria":"Expected outcome: with the server started in one shell and `./bin/speclang stop` issued from another, the serving process exits 0 and prints no Error: ENOENT trace. Harness: start --port 39124, curl the dashboard for 200, stop, then assert the start process exit code is 0 and grep for ENOENT in its output is empty. Also covers stop-when-already-stopped (pid file absent) as a no-throw path with a unit test.","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-16T06:52:26Z","detail":{"metadata":{"provenance":"created_at stamped during provenance repair (row write was unpaired)","tick":"speclang-dogfood-2026-11-16-05-02-33"},"evidence":[{"run_id":"42e4c349","ts":"2026-11-16T16:04:29.475576+00:00"}]},"id":"DF-SPECLANG-6","priority":"P3","reasoning":"Dogfood 2026-11-16, fresh clone HEAD 2ace9a06, node v22.22.3. Repro: `./bin/speclang start --port 39124` (serves HTTP 200, dashboard title SpecLang Dashboard), then `./bin/speclang stop`. The start process dies with an uncaught exception: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, unlink .speclang/daemon.pid, thrown at Module.unlinkSync (node:fs:1948:11) from process.shutdown (dist/src/daemon/index.js:70:12). Reproduced twice (ports 39123 and 39124). Cause: process.shutdown unlinks the pid file unconditionally, but `speclang stop` already removed it, so the still-live server throws on its own exit path and exits non-zero with a red stack trace. The daemon itself works (after stop, `daemon status` reports Stopped), so this is friction on every normal start/stop cycle rather than data loss.","status":"complete","title":"P3 — `speclang stop` crashes the serving process with an uncaught ENOENT on .speclang/daemon.pid instead of a clean shutdown","type":"bug","foreman_note":"wave dispatch tick SpecLang-foreman-2026-11-16-14-19-15: worker in own worktree (base origin/main 4c66e6fd)\n\nmerged as a61ac6980a6e05bbf8d1d612bb5b6ff7acc2ce93 on origin/main; gitreins tier1 PASS + tier2 PASS (run 42e4c349); note DF-SPECLANG-9 also