 {"id":"DF-SPECLANG-014","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":"bug","complexity":3,"title":"P0 pipeline executor module missing from daemon.spec.dir tree - daemon cascade can never generate; plus 30s infinite recascade on permanent failure (DF-SPECLANG-2-R5 live repro)","reasoning":"LIVE REPRO 2026-11-16 (agent-driver baseline test, trilogy2 project): daemon detected the injected spec, convergence fired every 30s but every cycle logged: Pipeline execution error: Cannot find module /home/kara/speclang/specs/daemon.spec.dir/pipeline/executor.js imported from specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts - then Auto-recascade enabled - arming for next cascade, looping indefinitely with Files: 0 and Cascade complete false-success messages. Confirms DF-SPECLANG-2-R5 (never idles) and adds the root cause candidate: the executor module is absent from the spec tree the generated daemon imports from.","acceptance_criteria":"Expected outcome: with the repo built via npm run build, start the daemon plus coordinator against a scratch project whose specs directory gains a new .spec.md file; the run must return exit 0 with no 'Cannot find module' error for the pipeline executor, at least one non-empty generated file on disk, and the daemon must reach idle within 60 seconds of the last event. For the backoff half: break the executor deliberately, rerun the same scenario, and expect zero consecutive recascade cycles after the third failure plus status idle in the daemon state file. Proof: both daemon logs and the state file contents go in the row evidence.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"97fe99a4439ae1f025ac3b782f5dcbb14698a674be1d62e874118b5685d4a144","evidence":[{"run_id":"DF-SPECLANG-014","ts":"2026-11-16T19:07:39.981422+00:00"}]},"capability_tags":[],"created_at":"2026-11-16T17:15:20.595891+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T19:07:39.981422+00:00","foreman_note":"FIXED 2026-11-16 (agent, live-verified). Root causes: (1) specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts lazily imported '../pipeline/executor.js' which resolved to a nonexistent dir - src/daemon/daemon.ts is a SYMLINK to the spec-tree copy, so relative paths diverge per layout; fixed with a candidate-chain dynamic import (../../pipeline.spec.dir + ../../specs/pipeline.spec.dir) that works under tsx-from-specs, tsx-from-src and compiled dist. (2) pipeline.spec.dir/src/{executor,types}.ts imported '../daemon/types' which did not exist; repointed to daemon.spec.dir/src/types.js + added tsconfig paths aliases pipeline.spec.dir/src/* and daemon.spec.dir/src/*. (3) empty on_converge (no build.yaml) 'succeeded' with 0 stages - silent no-op; now returns success:false with a loud 'No pipeline stages configured' error. (4) DF-SPECLANG-2-R5 backoff: consecutive pipeline failure counter; at 3 the daemon stops auto-recascading, sets status error, prints a loud banner, and no longer reports false 'Cascade complete'. (5) watcher creates missing watch dirs instead of silently watching nothing. LIVE VERIFICATION: tril-final project with build.yaml (stage run: echo >> generated/pipeline-ran.txt): touch -> File event -> converge -> Stage SUCCESS -> non-empty generated file -> daemon-state status idle. Bare project: honest failure, backoff at 3 strikes, status error, loop stopped. npm run build clean; targeted vitest 3/3. Commits: see board events."}
